BUG REPORT FROM USER: 'I use a default map to turn a boolean flag on by default, but the help text does not reflect it. With this command:

    @click.command()
    @click.option("--name/--no-name", is_flag=True, show_default=True)
    def foo(name):
        click.echo(name)

running foo with default_map={"foo": {"name": True}} correctly prints True, yet `foo --help` still says `default: no-name`. I expected the help to say `default: name`, matching the value the flag actually takes. The help text seems to ignore the default map and only look at the flag own default.'

Your job: find the root cause (look at src/click/core.py Option.get_help_record / Option.get_default / Parameter.get_default / Parameter.consume_value / Context.lookup_default and how the default_map is consulted; the help record likely calls get_default(ctx) without the default_map being applied, or looks at self.default directly), fix it minimally in the source, and verify. Also check the docs in /click/docs (options.rst, parameters.rst, api docs) and docstrings for what show_default and the default map are documented to do.

IMPORTANT CONSTRAINTS: (a) Do NOT modify or delete any pre-existing test in /click/tests; pre-existing green tests must keep passing. (b) Only fix this bug; no unrelated changes. (c) No internet. (d) Record the baseline first: `cd /click && python -m pytest tests -q` (and/or a pristine copy `git -C /click archive HEAD | tar -x -C /tmp/pristineC`). Then implement the fix and re-run the full suite. Write throwaway scripts under /tmp (NOT in the repo) reproducing the user's exact case with CliRunner(default_map=...) and `--help`, and confirm the help shows `default: name` while the value is True; also test the `--no-name`/False case, a non-flag option with a default_map value and show_default, default_map with a callable default, and a default_map given on a group/subcommand. Report back: root cause, exact file+lines changed, the diff of your change only, test results (baseline vs after), and any pre-existing failures observed.
